    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for gnome-remote-desktop.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "GNOME Remote Desktop is a remote desktop and screen sharing service for the GNOME desktop environment.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* gnome-remote-desktop: Busy-Wait DoS in VNC TLS I/O Handlers (GNUTLS_E_AGAIN / GNUTLS_E_INTERRUPTED) (CVE-2026-109832)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
